// Tower Compiler: editable compiler, interpreter, host and LLVM backend source.
// import tower resolves the project file tower.tower, not the compiler binary.
// Its ordinary imports load foundation.tower and then bedrock.tower.
// The running compiler builds the next compiler generation from these files.
// Rebuild compiler compiles each import unit and links fresh Wasm reactors.
// New compiler generations are tested before use; Reset compiler recovers the original.
// Transitional native support still supplies adapters/runtime and upstream LLVM/LLD.
// Continue adding ports to Compose*.cmake and removing their native target sources.
// The endpoint is all project-owned code in Tower with standalone build recipes.

// Compiler build unit. Imports define its complete source closure.
// Add newly ported .tower modules to the owning CMake import manifest;
// the published project follows it. Browser edits to these imports also rebuild.
